blocks.en:
Figure 5: Qualitative comparison on bidirectional few-step T2V generation. Both compared methods are distilled from the same HunyuanVideo-1.5 backbone.
Each pair shows the DMD student (top) and SF 2 (bottom) on the same prompt and noise;
a zoomed crop on the right of each panel highlights the rendered text. Across all four prompts, SF 2 produces sharp, legible glyphs where DMD collapses into blurred or scrambled characters, indicating that the rep loss strengthens the student’s spatial representation.

blocks.zh:
图5:双向几步T2V生成的定性比较. 这两种比较方法都从同一个HunyuanVideo-1.5骨干中蒸馏出来.
每对都显示DMD的学生(顶部)和SF 2(底部)在同一迅速和噪音上;
每个面板右侧的缩放块突出显示文本。 SF 2在所有四个提示中,都会产生尖锐,清晰的格言,其中DMD崩溃成模糊或模糊的字符,表明代表损失会增强学生的空间代表性.
